# The landing page is the static `site/` directory and nothing is built on
# Vercel (vercel.json: no framework, no build, outputDirectory "site"), so the
# CLI has no reason to upload the rest of the repository. Without this file,
# `vercel deploy` walks the whole checkout — Gradle outputs, `.claude/`
# worktrees, anything not in its short built-in ignore list — and trips the
# 15,000-file upload limit. Ignore everything, then allow back only what the
# deployment reads.
*
!site
!site/**
!vercel.json
!.vercelignore
